{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Representation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"indexed mesh representation indexed mesh representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Representation.md","fileName":"Indexed Mesh Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Indexed Mesh Representation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Portable 3D Model Data]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Portable 3D Model Data","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Representation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"indexed mesh representation indexed mesh representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Representation.md","fileName":"Indexed Mesh Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Indexed Mesh Representation","heading":"Indexed Mesh Representation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An indexed mesh stores each reusable vertex once and defines faces by referring to positions in that vertex list. Normals and texture coordinates may have their own indexed collections, allowing the representation to share data where appropriate.\n\nCompared with a naive specification that repeats every triangle's coordinates, indexing can substantially reduce file size and reveal which faces share geometric points. It also introduces ordering dependencies: a face remains meaningful only while its indices correspond to the intended entries in the referenced lists.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Portable 3D Model Data","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Indexed Mesh Represent